        "timestamp": 1777368842,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Iran offers to reopen Strait of Hormuz if US lifts its blockade and the war ends Issued on: 28/04/2026 - 11:34 Iran offered to end its chokehold on the Strait of Hormuz if the US lifts its blockade on the country and ends the war in a proposal that would postpone discussions on the Islamic Republic's nuclear program, two regional officials said Monday. US President Donald Trump seems unlikely to accept the offer, which was passed to the Americans by Pakistan and would leave unresolved the disagreements that led the US and Israel to go to war on Feb. 28. Lebanon health ministry says Israeli strikes kill 4 in south despite ceasefire 28/04/2026 Tuareg rebels and jihadists in control of key Mali town after offensive 28/04/2026 Train collision in Indonesia kills 14, injures dozens 28/04/2026 Britain's King Charles meets Trump in bid to salvage ties 28/04/2026 Italian Crans-Montana victims angered over Swiss hospital bills 28/04/2026 Musk lawsuit against OpenAI 'more about corporate strategy than any philosophical or ethical moves' 28/04/2026 Technology Mali's tale of two insurgencies: 'Jihadists seek caliphate while Tuareg rebels pursue autonomy' 27/04/2026 Africa US 'used to' school shootings: Gun violence 'inevitably turned to the political arena as well' 27/04/2026 Americas Syria tries prominent Assad-era security official 27/04/2026 Middle East"
